## Explicitly deferred integration items

These findings are real but belong to later plan owners and were not implemented here:

- Task 6 must supply the archive reducer, campaign-CAGR recomputation, zero-trade eligibility,
  top-K admission, novelty key, and target-gap authority. Task 5 stores the complete inputs/outcomes
  and refuses to invent a competing policy.
- Task 7/8 must persist and role-bind the issued investigator/critic evidence artifacts, add typed
  stage-specific provider/runtime failure facts, and wire event/record/checkpoint calls into the
  authorized runtime. Generic supplemental artifact refs remain available, but Task 5 does not
  fabricate later role-envelope types.
- The evaluator's baseline/candidate policy-identity convention, V3 client surface/default, and
  evaluator source-map omissions are separate evaluator/runtime defects. They require focused
  changes outside this task's three-file scope.
- Semantic fingerprints intentionally exclude source/policy identity per Task 4. The immutable
  experiment record binds the suite fingerprint to the revision that produced it; it never upgrades
  suite-local equivalence to global equivalence.

