## Review correction

The three review findings were reproduced and corrected within the original three-file boundary:

- The public `is_testable_experiment_status_v5` predicate defines the final matrix. Invalid,
  exact-duplicate, and suite-local behavioral-equivalent records are finalizable but untestable and
  reject critic fields. Quick-rejected, zero-trade, timed-out, cancelled, evaluation-failed, and
  evaluated records are testable and require both their exact review and full critic-artifact
  reference at construction. Repository append/load repeats this gate, authenticates the canonical
  content-addressed critic, and proves exactly one embedded review match before a record can be
  created or returned.
- Checkpoint publication and recovery group checkpoint-authorized records by round. Every testable
  record in a round must share one critic artifact, and that artifact's unique review-ID set must
  exactly equal the round's testable record-ID set. Raw journal loading deliberately remains able to
  observe a crash-partial batch, but no partial/split/extra-review batch can become checkpoint
  authority.
- `ArtifactRefV5` now applies the repository's portable component grammar at contract construction:
  every component rejects ADS colons, Windows device basenames, trailing dot/space, non-ASCII or
  otherwise unsupported characters, overlength names, and noncanonical POSIX structure.
- Investigator projection now requires `selected_parent_record_ref`. A non-null reference must be
  one of the supplied checkpoint-authorized records, have evaluated status, bind the requested
  selected revision, and represent a non-no-op producer; null explicitly denotes an external or
  baseline parent and creates no journal-derived ancestry. Revision ownership is list-valued,
  same-revision feedback is preserved in deterministic root-to-selected group order, and conflicting
  parent lineage or immutable revision identity fails with a typed ambiguity. Exact-duplicate and
  unpromoted records can contribute feedback but cannot advance ancestry.

